@startuml fleet-shell-tool-windows-state
title Tool-window visibility (per window: Project / Claude / Bottom)

[*] --> Open : default on launch\n(session-only, not persisted)

Open --> Closed : click rail icon\n(toggle_tool_window)
Closed --> Open : click rail icon again

state "Bottom window only" as BottomSub {
  Open --> Open : ToggleFindToolWindow/RunToolWindow/\nProblemsToolWindow while a DIFFERENT\nbottom_view tab is active\n(switches tab, forces open, does not close)
}

Open --> Hidden_by_Zen : ToggleZenMode on
Closed --> Hidden_by_Zen : ToggleZenMode on
Hidden_by_Zen --> Open : ToggleZenMode off\n(restores exactly the prior flag)
Hidden_by_Zen --> Closed : ToggleZenMode off\n(restores exactly the prior flag)

note right of Hidden_by_Zen
  Zen Mode is a display-only override,
  not a state reset: the underlying
  show_*_tool_window flag is untouched.
end note
@enduml
